PolicyManagerCommitSetupTest
├── When the nonce is not the current one plus one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce carrying the supplied and the expected nonce, including for a nonce another write already moved past.
├── When the commitment is zero
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_InvalidCommitment carrying the zero commitment.
├── When the commitment is the commitment of an empty body at the nonce the write will hold
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_InvalidCommitment carrying that commitment.
├── When the nonce is wrong and the commitment is invalid
│   └── It should revert with either PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce or PolicyManager_InvalidCommitment.
├── When no setup exists
│   ├── It should store the commitment under nonce one.
│   ├── It should write the current block as setupCommittedAtBlock.
│   ├── It should leave the next attempt id at one.
│   └── It should emit SetupCommitted alone with both metadata fields.
├── When a setup exists
│   ├── It should replace the commitment and move the nonce by exactly one.
│   ├── It should write the block of the new write.
│   └── It should emit SetupCommitted alone.
├── When the setup was cleared
│   └── It should continue the nonce from the clear rather than rewind it.
├── When two writes land in one block
│   └── It should move the nonce once per write and emit one event per write.
├── When the action is any address that serves the account
│   ├── It should store the commitment under that action.
│   └── It should emit SetupCommitted alone for that action.
├── When the action serves the account
│   ├── It should ask the action supportsAccount for the caller, by a static call and nothing else.
│   ├── It should store the commitment.
│   └── It should emit SetupCommitted alone.
├── When the action reads the manager while answering
│   └── It should ask before the attempt is cancelled and before the setup is written.
├── When the action has no code
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the actions supportsAccount reverts
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action answers false
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns no data
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns less than one word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns more than one word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns a word other than one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns two words whose first is one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns one word with its only set byte other than the last
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action returns a word whose low byte is one but is not one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
├── When the action writes state while answering
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_ActionDoesNotServeAccount carrying the caller and the action, and change nothing.
│   └── It should leave the action's storage unwritten.
├── When the stored nonce is the largest uint64
│   └── It should revert with the arithmetic overflow panic and change nothing.
├── When the block number is the largest uint48
│   ├── It should store the commitment under nonce one.
│   └── It should store the largest uint48 as setupCommittedAtBlock.
├── When the block number is past the width of the block field
│   ├── It should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast carrying the width and the block number.
│   └── It should change nothing.
├── When an attempt is waiting
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Cancelled and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptCancelled with a zero canceller before SetupCommitted.
│   ├── It should leave the attempt counter where it was.
│   └── It should reach no method and no pause read, only the action's own supportsAccount.
├── When the last attempt is no longer waiting
│   └── It should emit SetupCommitted alone and leave the record untouched.
├── When an attempt waits under another action
│   └── It should leave that attempt waiting.
└── When an address other than the account calls
    ├── It should write only that address's own setup.
    └── It should leave the account's setup and waiting attempt untouched.
